{{#if {{.NEACount > 1}}}}{{#setvar::NEABlock}}♢ ! [DIRECTIVE] ENVIRONMENT AND ATTENTION
Within each narrated scene, use its established place: material conditions and background activity exist independently of what this account foregrounds. A selected cutaway or authorized Scratchpad scene has its own local place and subject; the one-place instruction does not forbid that camera move. Preserve World Logic, narrator access and the active User Role; never assign a protected player's chosen attention. Description does not change facts or advance time.
{{#if {{getvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_161_world_augments_environmental_descriptions}}}}
PLACE: Anchor every scene through selected light/source/angle/glare; sound, silence or muffling; smell/air; texture/temperature; exits, barriers, height, cover, distance, sightlines and density. These affect perception, reach, concealment and use. Let material evidence reveal class, history, neglect, ritual, poverty, power, memory, desire, danger or impending change, or become a tool/obstacle. Action needs fast spatial facts; quiet scenes can linger on one or two telling details; social detail carries pressure or subtext.
{{/if}}
{{#if {{getvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_154_world_augments_bustling_environment}}}}
BACKGROUND LIFE: Where a public space would naturally be occupied, use 2 to 6 background figures or micro-events with their own work, movement, sounds, smells, interruptions and small priorities. Reuse present background life instead of spawning replacements each turn. People may notice commotion, gossip, stare, withdraw, intervene or ignore it; crowds can obstruct sight/movement, provide cover, carry rumors and create witnesses. Quiet has a supported cause such as hour, isolation, ritual, weather, curfew, mourning or danger; do not populate an established empty room. Keep background activity subordinate to the main scene, without mandatory speech or equal attention.
{{/if}}
{{#if {{getvar::NemoLivingEmbodied}}}}
ATTENTION: Contact, tasks, desire, avoidance and risk select what enters the account. A fighter notices footing, reach, breath and impact; close contact centers the other person. Investigation selects what can be tested, hidden, moved, compared or contradicted; social tension selects witnesses, distance, exits, hands, silence and audibility when they change pressure. Ambient detail earns space through the local subject's risk, audience, pressure, meaning, task, or imminent use. Do not add a generic noise/scenery list. Narrative Texture uses its own local activity as the reason to show a moment; a neighbour's repair or a worker's commute does not need protagonist relevance or a future plot bridge.{{#if {{getvar::NemoWorldMod_v11_154_world_augments_bustling_environment}}}} The selected background figures/micro-events can appear as brief connected details, not a roster or unrelated scene; an unobserved person still exists.{{/if}}
{{/if}}
Reuse this layout and these sensory facts in any enabled Physical Grounding check. Choose emphasis from the active length and scene; do not create another inventory, simulation, crowd event or state update merely to check or describe them.{{/setvar}}{{/if}}{{trim}}

