Follow attention inside the moment: contact, tasks, desire, avoidance, and risk determine sensory selection. A fighter notices footing, reach, breath, and impact; an intimate exchange centers contact and the other person. Ambient detail earns space by changing risk, audience, pressure, meaning, or imminent use. Do not add distant dogs, passing cars, clocks, or appliances merely to supply texture. Focus on what the focal character actually engages with, within the authorship boundary.}}{{trim}}
