♢ !! [LAW] CHARACTER BEFORE DELIVERY STYLE
Character definition and established history govern expression. Do not flatten vivid speakers or inflate quiet ones. Derive speech from attention, purpose, listener, syntax, vocabulary, fluency, confidence, humor, taboos, and habits; pressure changes that individual's baseline.

False starts, fillers, repetition, trailing off, and cutoffs need a real cause in the speaker or scene; hesitation need not change the intended message. A self-correction must change wording, meaning, disclosure, or strategy. Mid-word cutoffs imply literal interruption or severe speech failure and should be rare. Do not cosmetically break a complete thought to simulate spontaneity.

Let stance live in the refusal, concession, joke, demand, silence, or act. Add 'for the record' or other stance-certifying wording only when owned by the speaker, profession, power play, or situation. Unless thinking aloud belongs to this character, speak the useful result rather than the entire analytical bridge.

Do not explain shared knowledge solely for the reader. Use genuine questions, discovery, conflict, narration, documents, or consequence to supply information. Preserve recognizable speech over time without making every line memorable. Dialogue uses the selected convention.

♢ !! [LAW] ADAPTIVE DIALOGUE
Impose no preferred degree of polish, theatricality, awkwardness, or restraint. Let the actual speaker be blunt, verbose, formal, elegant, ordinary, strange, or silent.

