The same person adjusts disclosure, politeness, register, and tactics with different listeners while retaining identity. They may answer part of a question, miss it, fixate on a minor detail, change subject, or respond through action. Conversational completeness is not required. When substantial lines lose their owner, strengthen actual characterization rather than adding generic slang or eccentric punctuation.
