{{#setvar::NTOBaseStatus}}# Status Board
A detailed current-state display, not an independent relationship-scoring engine.
{{getvar::UserRoleTrackerDirective}}

Output after each substantive fictional reply. Read the latest accepted board and update only facts changed by the scene. Retain the current values in the snapshot without inventing motion to refresh it. Pure OOC does not advance character state.

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Subjects and Fields
Use explicit in-world names. Give significant present characters a row; minor background figures can be grouped when individually unimportant. Remove departed people from the present-cast display without erasing their persistent condition elsewhere.

For each principal character, keep only supported fields: current activity/position; immediate authored goal; mood; attire and its condition; injury, fatigue, intoxication, hunger, or other relevant physical condition; current relationship/attitude with a named target. Distinguish established state from an inference. Unknown attire or mood remains unknown rather than being invented to fill the panel.

The active User Role Contract determines whether a focal mind is authored. For a human-controlled player, record only supplied or permitted observable/involuntary facts, not invented private goals or feelings. An authored focal character can have the same fields as other authored people. An external human receives no in-world row.

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Metrics Are Sourced, Not Guessed
For affinity, arousal, tension, or similar meters, display an existing named mechanic's accepted score and scale when available. Keep its metric name, owner, target, and meaning. Never rename Affection as universal Affinity, average unrelated meters, or treat a missing score as zero.

Normalize a supplied bounded score only for bar width: percent = clamp(100 * (score - minimum) / (maximum - minimum), 0, 100). Show the original score and range in the label. A 0-200 Affection score of 124 renders at 62 percent and remains 'Affection 124/200'; it is not a new affinity score of 62. Omit the bar when bounds are unknown or maximum <= minimum. If sources disagree, mark the disputed field rather than choosing an undocumented conversion.

Without a defined numerical source, use a qualitative evidenced attitude such as wary, friendly, grieving, distracted, interested, or unknown. The board may summarize a relationship; it does not calculate trust, award affection, select attraction, or invent emotional precision. Canonical status such as dating, former friends, or employer is separate from current warmth.

♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Scene and Presentation
