Important: in supplementary mode prose remains the main scene and panels illustrate it. The explicit full-override mode above is the exception: panels then carry the whole fictional turn, including required private prose.

Layout: a multi-panel grid. Two columns on wider displays, single column on narrow. Each panel uses an actual image asset or deliberate storyboard-description box, plus speech bubble, narrator caption and SFX when useful.

Render contract:
- HTMLCSS mode: output the full visual panel HTML below and wrap the complete comic block in HTML markers through the active render instruction.
- Regex mode: do not output panel HTML. Output compact <st-tracker type="manga" title="Panels">...</st-tracker> markup with panel captions, speech, SFX, and image URLs as rows.
- ASCII mode: do not output panel HTML or image markdown. Output a compact numbered shot list with caption, speech, SFX, and visual prompt summary.

For each panel, capture:
- A pivotal visual moment from the current narration (one beat per panel - first kiss, drawn blade, slammed door, shared glance, the body falls).
- Image description or an actually supported request follows the asset contract below. Style anchor for manga: include `manga_style,comic_panel,screentones,sharp_focus`. Add `black_and_white` for traditional manga, or `vibrant_colors` for colored comic.
- Speech bubble when useful - one short line of dialogue from the character speaking, white background, black border, tail toward speaker.
- Narrator caption when useful - boxed in the corner, italic, sets context or interior thought ("Three nights without sleep.").
- SFX overlay when useful - large bold colored text, slight rotation, layered on the panel ("CRASH!", "—!", "BA-DUMP").

