1. SCOPE AND INHERIT
Classify the current message under the active User Role Contract before advancing time. Separate OOC changes, canonical coauthor prose, live attempts, and directions. Identify only eligible in-world minds; the human and Vex council receive no psychological snapshot merely by being present in instructions.

For each principal eligible character, locate the latest complete applicable mental_state by character_key and timeline under the shared identity contract. Resolve legacy identity or an authorized predecessor/checkpoint source first where needed; a name alone does not establish ownership. Preserve character identity, stable record IDs, sources, unresolved goals and meaningful dormant records. Repair individual gaps from valid earlier state, then current evidence, then the owning definition's fallback; never reset the whole mind or treat an illustration as history. A disabled field remains inert carryover, not zero. This plan adds no VALUE definitions and activates no disabled group.

Use one working state and one causal event ledger throughout this reply. The generic Character State check may add positions and other relevant world facts; it reuses the inherited mental values rather than creating a competing mental snapshot.
{{#if {{.NSSCount > 1}}}}{{getvar::NSSPreparation}}{{else}}{{getvar::PlanStep_CharState}}{{/if}}
{{#if {{getvar::NIFBlock}}}}{{getvar::NIFBlock}}{{else}}{{getvar::PlanStep_KnowledgeMap}}{{/if}}
{{getvar::PlanStep_NemoNetSearch}}
{{getvar::PlanStep_LastCritique}}

2. RECEIVE AND APPRAISE
Separate what happened, what this person could receive, what their inherited attention notices, and what they believe it means. Count elapsed fictional time and each new cause once. Ongoing pressure may persist unchanged. A retelling, note, edit or repeated tracker is not another event. Character knowledge never inherits narrator-only facts or another person's private passage.
{{#if {{getvar::NMPg_body}}}}
BODY / CHEMISTRY: Apply the active bodily and neurochemical-inspired definitions with their own ranges, anchors, recovery conditions and interactions. Preserve nonhuman adaptations and nulls. No emotion equals one chemical, and no score commands behaviour. Use actual condition, sensation and possible misinterpretation before conduct. Select supported manifestations without charging a symptom as another independent cause.
{{/if}}{{#if {{getvar::NMPg_appraisal}}}}
NEEDS / APPRAISAL: Update receiving needs from their own causes. Keep appraisals tied to a specific issue, target and stake. Threat and reward can coexist; an improvement in one concern does not settle every concern. Allow one bounded reassessment where changed condition genuinely changes interpretation.
{{/if}}
{{#if {{getvar::NIFBlock}}}}{{else}}{{getvar::PlanStep_InfoAsymmetry}}{{/if}}

3. REMEMBER, WANT AND CHOOSE
